          <h2>What's actually at risk <span class="highlight">right now</span></h2>
          <p>Insurance advice that ignores your life stage is just a sales pitch. Pick the one that sounds like you.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="persona-picker" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose your life stage">
          <button class="persona-card" role="tab" id="persona-tab-genz" aria-controls="persona-panel-genz"
            aria-selected="true" data-persona="genz">
            <span class="icon-tile"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-briefcase"></use></svg></span>
            <span class="persona-age">Age 22–28</span>
            <h3>Just started earning</h3>
            <p>First job, first salary — and cover that quietly belongs to your employer, not to you.</p>
          </button>

          <button class="persona-card" role="tab" id="persona-tab-newparent" aria-controls="persona-panel-newparent"
            aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-persona="newparent">
            <span class="icon-tile teal"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-baby"></use></svg></span>
            <span class="persona-age">Age 28–38</span>
            <h3>New or expecting parent</h3>
            <p>A second person now depends on your income, and the clock on maternity waiting periods has already
              started.</p>
          </button>

          <button class="persona-card" role="tab" id="persona-tab-sandwich" aria-controls="persona-panel-sandwich"
            aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-persona="sandwich">
            <span class="icon-tile warm"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-users"></use></svg></span>
            <span class="persona-age">Age 45–60</span>
            <h3>Kids and parents to cover</h3>
            <p>You are holding up two generations at once — and you are the single point of failure for both.</p>
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Panel: Gen-Z ─────────────────────────────── -->
        <div class="persona-panel active" id="persona-panel-genz" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="persona-tab-genz">
          <div class="persona-panel-head">
            <h3>You are covered — until the day you resign</h3>
            <p>Group cover from your employer feels like a solved problem. It is the single most common gap we fix,
              because it disappears exactly when your income does.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="persona-panel-body">
            <div class="pain-list">
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-briefcase"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Your group cover ends the day you leave</h4>
                  <p>Employer health cover is not portable. It does not follow you to the next job, it does not cover
                    you through a notice period gap, and it ends immediately if you are laid off — which is the exact
                    moment a hospital bill would hurt most.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-users"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>You have aged off your parents' family floater</h4>
                  <p>Most family floaters drop dependent children at 25. Many people discover this at a claim, not at
                    renewal. If nobody has bought you a plan in your own name, you are uninsured and do not know it
                    yet.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-clock"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Waiting periods only start counting once you buy</h4>
                  <p>Every health policy makes you wait 2–3 years before pre-existing and named illnesses are covered.
                    Those years pass whether or not you have a policy — so the cheapest year to start serving them is
                    this one, while you are healthy and premiums are at their lowest.</p>
                  <span class="pain-stat">A 25-year-old pays ₹10,149/yr — the same cover at 45 costs several times
                    more</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <aside class="persona-aside">
              <h4>Plans that fit this stage</h4>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/abhi.png"
                    alt="Aditya Birla Health" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">Activ One MAX</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">Cheapest health cover on our list</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/bajajlife.png"
                    alt="Bajaj Life" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">Bajaj eTouch II</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">Cheapest ₹2 Cr term cover</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/nivabupa.png"
                    alt="Niva Bupa" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">ReAssure 2.0 Platinum+</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">Rewards buying young — locks in your entry age</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <a href="#compare" class="btn btn-primary" data-persona-jump="genz">Compare these plans</a>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Panel: New parent ────────────────────────── -->
        <div class="persona-panel" id="persona-panel-newparent" role="tabpanel"
          aria-labelledby="persona-tab-newparent">
          <div class="persona-panel-head">
            <h3>The cover has to exist before you need it</h3>
            <p>Maternity and newborn benefits are the one part of health insurance you cannot buy on demand. Almost
              every gap we see at this stage comes down to timing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="persona-panel-body">
            <div class="pain-list">
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-calendar"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Maternity waiting periods run 2–4 years</h4>
                  <p>You have to buy the cover well before you start planning, not once you are expecting. None of the
                    five plans we rate covers maternity in its base policy — HDFC ERGO offers it through the Parenthood
                    rider, and Aditya Birla needs a separate product entirely.</p>
                  <span class="pain-stat">Buy after conception and maternity is simply not covered</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-baby"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Newborns need cover from day one</h4>
                  <p>A newborn can be admitted to the NICU within hours of birth, and that is one of the most expensive
                    admissions in Indian healthcare. Cover for the child has to already be in place, structured
                    correctly, before the delivery.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-home"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Your term cover now has to clear 20 years of liability</h4>
                  <p>A child means roughly two decades of dependency, and for most people it arrives alongside a home
                    loan. The cover you bought as a single 25-year-old was not sized for either.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-scale"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Both spouses are usually under-covered</h4>
                  <p>Cover typically gets bought for the higher earner only. If the other parent is uninsured, the
                    household is still one event away from a crisis — including the cost of replacing unpaid care.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <aside class="persona-aside">
              <h4>Plans that fit this stage</h4>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/hdfcergo.png"
                    alt="HDFC ERGO" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">Optima Secure+</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">Parenthood maternity rider available</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/axismax.png"
                    alt="Axis Max Life" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">Smart Term Plan Plus</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">99.71% claim settlement — the highest in India</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/hdfclife.png"
                    alt="HDFC Life" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">Click2Protect Supreme Plus</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">Raises cover at childbirth, no fresh medicals</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <a href="#compare" class="btn btn-primary" data-persona-jump="newparent">Compare these plans</a>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Panel: Sandwich generation ───────────────── -->
        <div class="persona-panel" id="persona-panel-sandwich" role="tabpanel"
          aria-labelledby="persona-tab-sandwich">
          <div class="persona-panel-head">
            <h3>Two generations, one income, no margin for error</h3>
            <p>This is the hardest stage to insure and the one where getting the details wrong is most expensive.
              Senior-parent cover in particular rewards precision.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="persona-panel-body">
            <div class="pain-list">
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-alert-triangle"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Parents over 60 face co-pays, loading and full waiting periods</h4>
                  <p>Premiums rise steeply, insurers add a co-payment share, and pre-existing conditions — which most
                    people over 60 have — sit behind a 2 to 3 year wait. Which insurer you pick decides whether that
                    wait is two years or three.</p>
                  <span class="pain-stat">A senior couple costs ₹66,505–₹78,923/yr at ₹15 L cover</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-briefcase"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Your corporate floater will not take them</h4>
                  <p>Most employer plans either exclude parents outright or price them as a punitive add-on with thin
                    limits. And like all group cover, it ends the day you change jobs — taking your parents' only
                    protection with it.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-trending-up"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>Your kids' education corpus is exposed</h4>
                  <p>College costs are a fixed future liability sitting on a single income. Without term cover sized to
                    it, that corpus is the first thing that gets liquidated.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pain">
                <span class="icon-tile sm danger"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-users"></use></svg></span>
                <div>
                  <h4>You are the single point of failure for two generations</h4>
                  <p>Parents above you, children below, and both financially dependent on you continuing to earn. That
                    is the definition of a risk that has to be transferred rather than absorbed.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <aside class="persona-aside">
              <h4>Plans that fit this stage</h4>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/sbigeneral.png"
                    alt="SBI General" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">Super Health Platinum Infinite</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">2-year pre-existing wait — a full year less than the rest</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/hdfcergo.png"
                    alt="HDFC ERGO" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">Optima Secure+</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">Best claims record in health insurance</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="persona-plan">
                <span class="monogram has-logo"><img class="brand-logo" src="assets/logos/absl.png"
                    alt="Aditya Birla Sun Life" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy"></span>
                <div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-name">ABSL Super Term Plan</div>
                  <div class="persona-plan-meta">Critical illness cover built into the base plan</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <a href="#compare" class="btn btn-primary" data-persona-jump="sandwich">Compare these plans</a>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
